).
Statistics.
All cellular experiments were performed in at least 3 biologically independent experiments except for oxygraph experiments, which were performed in at least 6 biological replicates. Animal data were generated from 5 animals in each group. Data were expressed as mean ± SD unless specified, and groups were compared using 1-way ANOVA with Bonferroni’s post hoc analyses for quantitative data that were normally distributed and the Kruskal-Wallis test for skewed data. Details of the bioinformatics analyses, identifying temporal clusters, and integrating data sets are described in the section on unbiased approaches.
